#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188043 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/id #uuid "ea6a79c4-09fc-5ae9-9e92-e7bacd4939d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10340" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d405cc4f96436baa6a90b8b8632a105efe7875f296e800db9ae846c1ee9eb805.svg)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=-2\\big]$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, -2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{X|-2}=\\dfrac{3}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[X^2 \\,| \\, Y=y \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-2] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2]-{\\mu }_{X|-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{9}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{80}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188044 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/id #uuid "fef21fcb-bab6-5f33-a792-280e28a97f81" :question/math-academy-id "e-10341" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bf8474d75d3d2dd57797d05266e055ca830e4b3e42532d167f358140906a3b4d.svg)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=3\\big]$ given that the conditional probability density function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 3)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y|3}=\\dfrac{3}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y^2 \\,| \\, X=x \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=3] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{y}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }3{y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[3\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{-1}}{(-1)}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{y}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=3]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =3-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188045 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "acb4923c-ce04-5cd5-af01-2f078a18ceed" :question/math-academy-id "e-10342" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x), & 1\\le x\\le e,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x), & 1\\le x\\le e, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,\\big|\\, X=1 \\big]$ given that the corresponding expected value is $\\mu_{Y|1}=\\dfrac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}\\big[Y^2 \\,| \\, X=x \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\textrm E\\big[ Y \\,|\\, X = x \\big]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)} \\\\  & =2y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $1 \\leq x \\leq e, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Outside this domain, we have $f_{Y|X} (y \\,|\\, x) = 0.$\n\nNotice that $f_{Y|X} (y \\,|\\, x)$ does not depend on $x.$ Therefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db52af3-2d00-57fe-83ac-e1e4cabb425b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529806} {:answer/id #uuid "6716a6d3-11e8-5185-8a14-c81cf63f513b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529837} {:answer/id #uuid "a5022d84-3876-5770-bcec-f22b051278c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529988} {:answer/id #uuid "cde47949-e5a4-500e-82a8-40c11888b0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530097} {:answer/id #uuid "d6596022-5d1b-577f-a508-e5cb0a327c6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6716a6d3-11e8-5185-8a14-c81cf63f513b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529837} :answer-field/id #uuid "7186124f-248a-5608-b06b-90a979a094ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530305}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2866f3dd-6eaf-53a1-aed5-f4ad68a3ab1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-146395" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530439 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e9f2a9-81ff-5bf2-8e64-c7bc991f3484" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529670} {:answer/id #uuid "2ceee17a-2287-5109-a8d8-f493be416a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529677} {:answer/id #uuid "bd62a3ac-b098-5d99-ad5f-adfcc32787b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530052} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcd9ab7-cb20-58e2-8fc7-ff6db6d9d900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530054} {:answer/id #uuid "de9d1ae1-ead5-520e-9b15-48bcf7370d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdcd9ab7-cb20-58e2-8fc7-ff6db6d9d900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530054} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa2b95c2-4b35-5103-a6f9-67b22f583604" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25e1f7ba-cab0-5f7d-b69c-953924c5cba0" :question/math-academy-id "q-146760" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+y)}{4}, & 0<x\\le 2y,\\,\\,0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}, & 0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{7}{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3(x+y)}{4})}{3{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+y}{4{y}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0<x\\le 2y,\\,0<y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$ \n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{x+1}{4}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{(x+1)}{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4+\\frac{8}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{20}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-{(\\frac{7}{6})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}-\\frac{49}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7382e9bb-66e3-536f-bf47-96a851f09b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{384}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529874} {:answer/id #uuid "88e834ca-6b87-553a-a237-a4681d65ed06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{381}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529912} {:answer/id #uuid "a56625c4-5e98-548c-bea6-5d94c2fb908e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529992} {:answer/id #uuid "cb89ee2c-2a49-5be9-9e3b-ad09f4a34f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530091} {:answer/id #uuid "e6cbeb1a-1375-5455-b8f6-f5ce904eaab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{360}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a56625c4-5e98-548c-bea6-5d94c2fb908e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529992} :answer-field/id #uuid "de48ce71-ed4e-5a50-80fd-461f4a5c82ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b4c1a29-e4bc-58eb-ae8a-170f49cecb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-146761" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{14}\\sqrt{x}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{14}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{3}{14}{x}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{49}{x}^{7/2}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{49}(128-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}-{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{381}{49}-\\frac{3}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{378}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dd913af-0d4d-584f-bb88-dda0c4ba49dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{63}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529640} {:answer/id #uuid "491be78e-8f5c-5fda-ad13-feacd90c83d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529752} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1fdd49-b96a-5691-8015-a399cf64cdd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529760} {:answer/id #uuid "bc42e7b8-acd5-5885-b965-56dae0313424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530051} {:answer/id #uuid "e09649d9-9ba1-578c-809b-de4e41e98be6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc42e7b8-acd5-5885-b965-56dae0313424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530051} :answer-field/id #uuid "c39ce385-0fcd-519a-a701-e719a952cd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a618ef53-1eb4-5d7e-994a-cd43bde62157" :question/math-academy-id "q-146771" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{24}{7{x}^{4}}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-1}=\\frac{9}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{24}{7{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{24}{7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}[(-\\frac{1}{2})-(-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-1]-{\\mu }_{X|-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}-{(\\frac{9}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{7}-\\frac{81}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188724 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "820466ba-6f36-5d47-afef-0ee20288f099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186625} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fa1bcc-91b5-57e8-85ba-c02fe35e14e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186626} {:answer/id #uuid "cb641e71-4763-57b7-bdbf-54ac5c041138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186627} {:answer/id #uuid "f74163e9-f3d4-5fad-816e-1c659459e6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186628} {:answer/id #uuid "08a51dff-0f49-52c1-ab38-9208cc65b517" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb641e71-4763-57b7-bdbf-54ac5c041138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186627} :answer-field/id #uuid "2338bb54-2402-5bab-b83e-832eb2b270cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186624}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cefc73e-1ad2-58be-a1de-e39c1b293d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-146806" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}, & \\,x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-2]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-2}=\\frac{4}{3}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }4{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{-2}}{(-2)}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-2] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-2]-{\\mu }_{X|-2}^{2} \\\\  & =2-{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{16}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530488 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1489093e-e3a3-55f2-b8ea-f74432755e95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529620} {:answer/id #uuid "15dde4cf-3e00-5078-bcf3-4598e3e2c37b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529622} {:answer/id #uuid "a86c312b-7c26-5fa7-90ee-febf5e5c1ac4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529997} {:answer/id #uuid "b64ece9b-7dd8-5d15-a949-4a704a08d316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530036} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a364ff-fd0c-5130-ba2f-e616cd755bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6a364ff-fd0c-5130-ba2f-e616cd755bc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530192} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d192f2-fd61-50da-beb1-1728d446e7ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8cb1a10c-eb8d-5503-81eb-a44381451337" :question/math-academy-id "q-146807" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{3/2}}, & \\,4\\le x\\le 9 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=6.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=4] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{9}3\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3/2}]}_{4}^{9} \\\\  & =2(27-8) \\\\  & =38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=4]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =38-{6}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a70864-faa5-54be-a449-99d26ac3090c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529611} {:answer/id #uuid "4016d54d-03ed-5d80-9023-2a222b021197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529729} {:answer/id #uuid "421cf42f-466d-5bf8-b694-47753f0f385e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529734} {:answer/id #uuid "abd5352c-5d54-5e3c-8b55-15e577a50730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530008} {:answer/id #uuid "db75dada-7b81-542d-bf6b-9186ddf533e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abd5352c-5d54-5e3c-8b55-15e577a50730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530008} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cacacfd-fd44-50c7-9618-968db11d920d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "febad6f8-061f-513c-bf3e-fbe38a2e6b2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146867" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2-x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}-y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2-x-y)}{(\\frac{3}{2}-y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2x-2y}{3-2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{4-2x-2\\cdot 1}{3-2\\cdot 1}=\\frac{4-2x-2}{3-2}=2-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(2-2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4-3}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f185006-9954-5514-b577-4d8238b5f3a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529646} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd874c7-e528-5b1f-9ca7-6d9dd97ff023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{160}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529720} {:answer/id #uuid "48b37456-2b35-5ad7-b4cb-c1cd5bcf7bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{160}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529750} {:answer/id #uuid "eda5a28b-0e86-5d28-8ea2-d7a1062c5778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{40}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530175} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf07cfd-45b2-51de-9143-b4f7db4de0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{320}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf07cfd-45b2-51de-9143-b4f7db4de0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{320}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530205} :answer-field/id #uuid "61c27587-c036-5512-931c-7ba163299613" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37a3fb25-8245-5c86-91e5-a1e534022eb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-146976" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3x(1-{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{3}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x(1-{y}^{2})}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNotice that the factor of $x$ cancels out, leaving an expression that does not depend on $x.$ Therefore, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ has no effect:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3(1-{y}^{2})}{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-{y}^{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}[(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-{(\\frac{3}{8})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{9}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{320}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3817ce70-a3ff-5d76-a92e-d07723b9ee70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529708} {:answer/id #uuid "6a5f285e-8dc0-5c5d-9205-5077e2524a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529850} {:answer/id #uuid "9a4a8876-64da-599a-b333-8da10c7aac94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529960} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a515b3-38b4-574d-ab70-b455f36a3a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530111} {:answer/id #uuid "f91da311-0343-5a45-b221-265ed560e0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a4a8876-64da-599a-b333-8da10c7aac94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529960} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe95487d-a357-5109-9ec1-41b889997c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e74c735c-6d68-5fb5-ad5e-520e538fc830" :question/math-academy-id "q-146981" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3({x}^{2}y+y)}{2}}{\\frac{3(1+{x}^{2})}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}y+y)}{(1+{x}^{2})},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2({1}^{2}\\cdot y+y)}{(1+{1}^{2})}=2y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=1]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e1b3266-8abd-5a10-871e-4abc1fdc45fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529642} {:answer/id #uuid "70cf3fbb-1f23-5477-a624-77b52dc5dfa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529868} {:answer/id #uuid "83567d3e-a18e-59f5-8de5-33ca7b6f14ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529906} {:answer/id #uuid "8f5d62b3-e68e-5f3b-a602-8ee58debbe22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529928} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bcefcf-5fab-5be9-97ba-7dd8b81b7c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f5d62b3-e68e-5f3b-a602-8ee58debbe22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529928} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6856b8d-546d-52e0-bed7-386f3bdb5d0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "48276d5d-5662-5546-a559-258dff238b59" :question/math-academy-id "q-147052" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{1}{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|\\frac{1}{2}}=-\\frac{7}{12}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ is a function of $x.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $Y$ given $X=x$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-y}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the expression for ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2}-y)}{(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{1}{2}-y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{y}^{2}(\\frac{1}{2}-y)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}]-{\\mu }_{Y|\\frac{1}{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-{(-\\frac{7}{12})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-\\frac{49}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23beb7dd-cb27-516a-87c2-22187aecddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529656} {:answer/id #uuid "694824b2-68f4-5131-a788-8727d4006841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529847} {:answer/id #uuid "98abe252-a017-5e77-b742-868d2adf14cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529954} {:answer/id #uuid "a16fd62d-5444-5e85-96f9-c5d6c7412063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529980} {:answer/id #uuid "b3d991b4-30f6-52a1-afce-0bb0222c6615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{48}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "694824b2-68f4-5131-a788-8727d4006841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529847} :answer-field/id #uuid "dccf4473-8ce6-5a7b-9170-9d177e05cbfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59aca6d9-1752-57b6-a727-2d8a95f6602b" :question/math-academy-id "q-149357" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{7{x}^{5/2}}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{12}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{12}{7{x}^{5/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{12}{7\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{24\\sqrt{x}}{7}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{7}-\\frac{24}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=0]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}-{(\\frac{12}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{7}-\\frac{144}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34cc357a-5d15-5858-a9da-1fbed5a44025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529702} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7acdc3-b79c-540c-8876-d8d4ab0dc5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529807} {:answer/id #uuid "6726955f-fcbe-51ef-81c8-c5b97a0a797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529838} {:answer/id #uuid "78434c08-58fd-5864-98a8-e08d7e0b4b36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529886} {:answer/id #uuid "dda5e757-29ae-51d9-ac4e-1c47bef47985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda5e757-29ae-51d9-ac4e-1c47bef47985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530129} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e3e1ec-1b29-5e88-912e-1d47aa3d4d7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6104314b-b213-5403-b96a-2e0ddf20d4ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-149399" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}, & \\,x\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|5}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=5] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}3{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-3\\cdot {x}^{-1}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{3}{x}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=5] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=5]-{\\mu }_{X|5}^{2} \\\\  & =3-{(-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ac5a0b-682d-58ce-8d19-548dbcc7f74d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529706} {:answer/id #uuid "4afaae21-7107-5bfd-ad67-092f29f09b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529758} {:answer/id #uuid "89f5dd1b-92ab-5512-a96e-3f46933c72fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529916} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea6f873-9f56-50db-b46b-34cc9aa92655" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{56}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529972} {:answer/id #uuid "d83f26db-9776-52f9-ae64-5454e381d5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83f26db-9776-52f9-ae64-5454e381d5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{75}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530117} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24a3477-bac3-594c-9727-d90bcb135154" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "988b2bee-8b04-51ca-a9c5-c53fb0470471" :question/math-academy-id "q-149406" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{2{x}^{9/2}}, & \\,x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|-4}=\\frac{7}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-4] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2{x}^{9/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{2{x}^{5/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot {x}^{-3/2}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{7}{3{x}^{3/2}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=-4] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=-4]-{\\mu }_{X|-4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-{(\\frac{7}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}-\\frac{49}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{28}{75}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fb0d6fb-00d5-5de1-a313-8844185c3c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529684} {:answer/id #uuid "33418197-c818-5634-8bea-8cd2f392480a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529693} {:answer/id #uuid "3451d803-efd4-5f81-986a-440c80249e19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529699} {:answer/id #uuid "77877244-7515-5435-983f-d36e7965ce08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529883} {:answer/id #uuid "eafb00d8-0e70-5b61-9556-8adc6cb3395b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77877244-7515-5435-983f-d36e7965ce08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529883} :answer-field/id #uuid "649ea598-2503-50e9-9e7d-932e638f034c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530295}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa39286d-2046-5d16-b60c-2e22bf1173b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-149407" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}}, & \\,x\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=6]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|6}=-\\frac{6}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=6] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}{x}^{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}-6{x}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(-6)}{(-4)}\\cdot {x}^{-4}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2{x}^{4}}]}_{-\\infty }^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=6] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=6]-{\\mu }_{X|6}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-{(-\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa63b29-0409-5b18-83ab-8b4023056556" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{81}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529596} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9c8d26-f55d-57d5-82b3-aed3370cefe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529891} {:answer/id #uuid "c72df470-55dc-5ffb-9294-61de19e9549f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{54}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530081} {:answer/id #uuid "cd39717a-740f-51a4-af35-8d0e263f4e78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530095} {:answer/id #uuid "dd7eacc8-0ca8-5f80-8673-05ce828c5aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{144}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd7eacc8-0ca8-5f80-8673-05ce828c5aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{144}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530128} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b99b6c-e8bf-5475-94ee-9d603ea83a76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04b02bf9-cae6-594f-ac96-340afba92b08" :question/math-academy-id "q-149411" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4{y}^{13/4}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|-1}=\\frac{9}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=-1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{4{y}^{13/4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{4{y}^{5/4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{-5/4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot {y}^{-1/4}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt[4]{y}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-9) \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-2] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=-2]-{\\mu }_{Y|-2}^{2} \\\\  & =9-{(\\frac{9}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =9-\\frac{81}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{144}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
